<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pietro Doria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1380">1380</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pietro Doria (died 1380) was a Genoese admiral during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-chioggia">War of Chioggia</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. In August 1379 his fleet captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chioggia">Chioggia</a> at the southern edge of the Venetian lagoon, threatening Venice itself, but the Venetians under Vettor Pisani and Carlo Zeno blockaded the Genoese there. Doria was killed during the siege in early 1380, and the trapped Genoese force surrendered in June.</p></div>
